Package (replaces the USB 2nd/3rd packages): laptop main 66cb14e0 -> 56bbf785, 277 files. check_and_copy.ps1: SAME 0 / NEW 111 /
OLD 149 / LOCAL 17 / GONE 0; none of the 54 files the machine changed since 95c398b was classified NEW/OLD. EastSun approved the
apply 20260926. Backup before apply: D:\HT9045\_BACKUP_20260926_pre_56bbf785 (system/config/IniData/runcfg/HT9045_Log,
lastdata.dat MD5 checked); OLD originals in D:\HT9045\_integ_ioweb_update_bak_20260926_102620.

The 17 LOCAL files were three-way merged in 5 disjoint groups, each adversarially reviewed. Rule: every machine behaviour kept
(MT-E1..MT-FIX1a, IOWEB-P*, ONSITE-1; csystem.cpp IsIndexMotorOutOfPower = 8929d13), the laptop's changes added (W5-b teach motion
buttons, YES/NO + blocking ShowMyMessage waits, R33 HandlerSys IO_CARD_TYPE item 5, R46/R53 no RS232 torque port on HT9050, R61,
W2 gates incl. G03 / h4-G4, Steven C-route pages, LastSet tail fields, [BOOT] summary, M108, ZSafePos from ini, recipe.change...).
Resolutions needing EastSun's confirmation (//AI(W906-MERGE-56bbf785) at each):
- teach page 1203 jog uses the machine's golden jog (ExtDrive 1 + Acm_AxJog) and golden's jog-family speed: Motor Test's last jog
  SetSpeed, and the teach page's own speed changes write it at a third of the value (uteach.cpp:1318 SetSpeed(Speed/3, true));
- ruling 6B (1203 axes ignore Direction) also applied to the machine's own new code (all-mode loop, GoldenMove1203, LastHomePos,
  Light Scale encoder); every PCI1203 row has Direction 0 today, so no change on this machine;
- the run gate (SystemStart) passes Motor Power (R9), formClose, and Motor Test STOP-direction requests only when Motor Test
  really has something to stop (a HOME / loop job, a running Light Scale); no fAllMotorHome clear while running;
- during a hand-teach, Motor Test's multi-axis / page-wide actions are refused (reloadMotorData, starting Light Scale, Motor Power,
  formShow, All-mode loop) and every motor of a request is checked;
- G03 (csystem.cpp ScanAllMotorStatus) is OPEN after the merge (laptop eed5033b; the machine had kept it closed; its reasons are
  stale after 8929d13) -- to be confirmed by EastSun.
Other review fixes: MbWait also runs golden DoAvoidIndexMotorFallDown; after a dialog answer the remaining commands of the same
drain go back to the carry (runnable) instead of being dropped; main.html gives the token back after recipe.change and the recipe
name stays visible when the list is refused; the recipe client's auth.* calls no longer acquire the token (server exempts auth.*;
main.html's authMode on load used to hold it for 10 minutes).
NOT done (open, for EastSun / Jimmy): (1) while a blocking dialog is open the 1203 monitor is not polled, so DI (EMG, SnMotorPower,
panel keys) is frozen until the answer -- needs a design ruling; (2) W906_Pci1203TorqueLimitHook is not installed (writes drive
SDO 60E0h/60E1h, needs EastSun's approval) -- with Model=9046_32GPIB (LS) the torque goes RS232 on [IndexDriver] COM11, which does
not exist on this PC, so START / Index auto report "Motor torque set error"; (3) machine identity (general.ini Model) left at
9046_32GPIB pending Jimmy; (4) the token-release package 0c1d5d0 is NOT applied (after using Motor Test, refresh the HMI before the
IO page); (5) the oracle line (build_integ_ora_ship_x86) was not rebuilt after the merge.
Build: build_integ_ship_x86 (WinLibs i686 16.2, C++14, shipping, HAVE_PCI1203) full build exit 0, 0 errors.
